1. A two-part packaging system, comprising:

a main housing defining a primary interior volume and having a dispenser positioned at a first end thereof;

a fluid insert disposed within the main housing, the fluid insert defining a secondary interior volume and comprising a breachable barrier isolating the secondary interior volume from the primary interior volume; 

a flexible end wall coupled to a second end of the main housing; and

a puncture tool integrated with an interior surface of the flexible end wall and extending inwardly toward the breachable barrier of the fluid insert,

wherein deformation of the flexible end wall from a first position to a second position drives the integrated puncture tool through the breachable barrier, establishing fluid communication between the secondary interior volume and the primary interior volume to allow fluid contained within the secondary interior volume to exit via the dispenser.
